*> PLB-C048 sort-procedure-no-record: a SORT INPUT PROCEDURE that never
*> RELEASEs a record, or an OUTPUT PROCEDURE that never RETURNs one.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SORTPROC.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO "sortwork".
    SELECT IN-A ASSIGN TO "in-a".
    SELECT IN-B ASSIGN TO "in-b".
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "out".
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
SD  SORT-FILE.
01  SORT-REC.
    05  SORT-KEY            PIC X(8).
    05  SORT-DATA           PIC X(72).
FD  IN-A.
01  IN-A-REC                PIC X(80).
FD  IN-B.
01  IN-B-REC                PIC X(80).
FD  OUT-FILE.
01  OUT-REC                 PIC X(80).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-EOF                  PIC X VALUE "N".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE SECTION.
BEGIN.
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-KEY
        INPUT PROCEDURE IS LOAD-RECORDS
        OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS WRITE-RECORDS
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-KEY
        INPUT PROCEDURE IS PREPARE THRU PREPARE-EXIT
        GIVING OUT-FILE
    SORT SORT-FILE ON DESCENDING KEY SORT-KEY
        USING IN-A
        OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS COUNT-ONLY
    MERGE SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-KEY
        USING IN-A IN-B
        OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS MERGED-OUT
    STOP RUN.
LOAD-RECORDS SECTION.
LOAD-START.
    OPEN INPUT IN-A
    PERFORM READ-ONE UNTIL WS-EOF = "Y"
    CLOSE IN-A.
READ-ONE.
    READ IN-A
        AT END MOVE "Y" TO WS-EOF
        NOT AT END PERFORM PASS-ON
    END-READ.
PASS-ON.
    RELEASE SORT-REC FROM IN-A-REC.
WRITE-RECORDS SECTION.
WRITE-START.
    OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE
    MOVE "N" TO WS-EOF
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = "Y"
        RETURN SORT-FILE INTO OUT-REC
            AT END MOVE "Y" TO WS-EOF
            NOT AT END WRITE OUT-REC
        END-RETURN
    END-PERFORM
    CLOSE OUT-FILE.
PREPARE SECTION.
PREPARE-START.
    MOVE SPACES TO SORT-REC.
PREPARE-EXIT.
    EXIT.
COUNT-ONLY SECTION.
COUNT-START.
    DISPLAY "SORTED".
MERGED-OUT SECTION.
MERGED-START.
    GO TO MERGED-READ.
MERGED-READ.
    RETURN SORT-FILE AT END CONTINUE END-RETURN.
